# Development Environment & Tooling

## Node.js Environment Setup
- **Node.js Version**: 20+ required (specified in [package.json](mdc:package.json) engines)
- **Package Manager**: Yarn (lockfile: [yarn.lock](mdc:yarn.lock))
- **Environment Variables**: Loaded via [next.config.js](mdc:next.config.js) with dotenv

### Environment Commands
```bash
# Use correct Node.js version
nvm use 20

# Install dependencies
yarn install

# Development server with Turbopack
yarn dev

# Build for production
yarn build

# Start production server
yarn start

# Linting
yarn lint

# Docker build
yarn build:docker
```

## Project Scripts and Commands

### Development Workflow
```bash
# Start development server with debugger and Turbopack
NODE_OPTIONS='--inspect' next dev --turbopack

# Build optimized production bundle
next build

# Start production server on port 8080
next start -p 8080

# Run ESLint
next lint

# Docker build for linux/amd64
docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t ghcr.io/conduitplatform/conduit-ui:latest .
```

### Git Workflow
```bash
# Prepare husky hooks
yarn prepare

# Generate changelog and tag release
yarn release

# Commit with conventional format (via commitizen)
npx cz
```

